# Semantic search endpoint. semanticSearchEnabled() requires this AND
# VITE_SEMANTIC_SEARCH === 'true' AND VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY — all three are
# set, and the feature is LIVE (see the block below).
#
# It lives here because its ABSENCE was a silent trap: flipping only
# VITE_SEMANTIC_SEARCH left the feature off with no error anywhere.
VITE_SEARCH_FN_URL=https://mrfblzsihpecockhsnqe.supabase.co/functions/v1/search

# Account deletion (GDPR Article 17), LIVE from 2026-08-14. The button in the
# sign-in section is hidden while this is absent, which it deliberately was until
# the destructive path had actually been executed once — a delete button that
# cannot delete is worse than none, because whoever presses it believes they are
# gone.
#
# Verified end to end against a real confirmed account before this line was
# added: user created and signed in, given a trip row and a public share, then
# account-delete returned 200 {"ok":true,"shares_deleted":1} and the user 404'd,
# with 0 trip rows and 0 share rows remaining. Guards were already verified
# separately — GET 405, no-auth 401, anon-key-as-bearer 401, garbage token 401.
#
# Rollback = delete this line and push. The function stays deployed and harmless;
# nothing can reach it without a user's own token.
VITE_ACCOUNT_DELETE_FN_URL=https://mrfblzsihpecockhsnqe.supabase.co/functions/v1/account-delete

# Search-by-meaning, LIVE from 2026-08-12. Prerequisites verified before flipping:
#   item_embeddings applied and populated (456 kB, one row per catalog item)
#   search function deployed and returning results
#   OPENAI_API_KEY set (2026-07-21); RATE_LIMIT_SALT set (2026-08-12)
#   Privacy Policy names OpenAI as a US sub-processor and the 30-day hash+vector
#
# Shipped BELOW its own quality bar, deliberately and on the record: the golden
# set scores 66% recall against the 80% target written into it. The shortfall is
# concentrated in NEGATION — "we get seasick" scores 0/3 and "no walking, we are
# tired" 1/3, because those sentences embed close to the very thing they rule
# out. Acceptable only because semantic hits are APPENDED below the substring
# results rather than replacing them, so a bad match costs a mediocre extra
# suggestion, not a wrong plan.
#
# Rollback is deleting the next line and pushing.
VITE_SEMANTIC_SEARCH=true

# Cookieless traffic beacon (src/lib/beacon.ts + supabase/functions/collect),
# turned on 2026-08-22 for the r/Aruba launch. Its ABSENCE is the off switch,
# the same shape as VITE_ACCOUNT_DELETE_FN_URL above.
#
# Why this and not VITE_POSTHOG_KEY, which is still deliberately empty: PostHog
# writes an identifier to the device, so under the 2026-08-13 ruling it needs
# consent and counts only the consented share of traffic. This beacon writes
# NOTHING to the device — identity is derived server-side from ip+ua+date and
# discarded — so it runs on legitimate interest and counts 100% of visitors.
# That is what makes "we sent you N people" quotable to a partner. Do not merge
# the two pipes; src/lib/beacon.ts says why at length.
#
# Prerequisites, and it stays inert until ALL of them are true:
#   ANALYTICS_SALT set (2026-08-22)
#   web_events applied (20260820090000 — the repo's later-dated duplicate was
#     deleted 2026-08-23; the table has existed since 08-20)
#   collect deployed WITHOUT jwt verification:
#     supabase functions deploy collect --no-verify-jwt
#   The flag is load-bearing. navigator.sendBeacon cannot set headers, so the
#   beacon sends no Authorization at all; deployed with the default
#   verify_jwt=true every call 401s silently and web_events stays empty with
#   nothing visibly wrong. contact-notify is the existing public precedent.
#
# Country is RESOLVED as of 2026-08-23: ip_country holds 706,484 DB-IP Lite
# ranges and collect asks country_for_ip at write time, keeping the two-letter
# code and discarding the address. Rows written before that date have no
# country and never can — the IP is not stored, so there is nothing to backfill
# from. In practice that is no loss: collect was not deployed until 08-23, so
# there are no such rows.
#
# Rollback = delete the next line and push. The function stays deployed and
# collects nothing, because nothing calls it.
VITE_COLLECT_FN_URL=https://mrfblzsihpecockhsnqe.supabase.co/functions/v1/collect

# Internal traffic dashboard endpoint, read by src/pages/Stats.tsx.
# NOT a secret: `stats` is gated on the ADMIN_UIDS allowlist and fails closed —
# an unset allowlist admits nobody — and stats_summary is REVOKEd from anon and
# authenticated, so this URL being public buys a stranger a 401 or a 403.
VITE_STATS_FN_URL=https://mrfblzsihpecockhsnqe.supabase.co/functions/v1/stats
